    "sections": [
      {
        "label": "1st quarter",
        "score": "BOS 34, WSH 28",
        "text": "Neemias Queta scored 13 points before Anthony Davis had any, and Tatum had 15 points and five assists in the quarter. Boston led 21–9 with 5:52 left and 34–28 after one."
      },
      {
        "label": "2nd quarter",
        "score": "BOS 80, WSH 49",
        "text": "The Celtics opened the quarter on a 14–3 run, capped by Payton Pritchard's three for a 48–31 lead at 9:02. A later 11–0 run with three Tatum threes made it 70–38 with 2:19 left; Boston made 10 threes in a 46-point quarter, and Tatum had 28 at the half."
      },
      {
        "label": "3rd quarter",
        "score": "BOS 104, WSH 89",
        "text": "Washington outscored Boston 40–24 and cut it to 94–81 on Bilal Coulibaly's dunk with 3:20 left. Paul George answered with a step-back three and Pritchard scored the next five for a 102–81 lead, before two Coulibaly threes and Trae Young free throws made it a 15-point game."
      },
      {
        "label": "4th quarter",
        "score": "Final: BOS 131, WSH 116",
        "text": "Davis and AJ Dybantsa led a Wizards push, and Dybantsa's bank shot made it 117–112 with 3:19 left. Tatum's layup made it 119–112, then Baylor Scheierman, scoreless until then, scored Boston's next eight: a three at 2:31, two free throws and a 30-footer for 127–114 with 1:16 left."
      }
